WEBVTT

00:16.057 --> 00:16.933
Run!

00:21.438 --> 00:22.313
Run. Fast!

00:45.920 --> 00:46.755
Hey!

00:50.467 --> 00:52.010
Fuck!

00:52.594 --> 00:53.428
Ditch the bag!

00:54.304 --> 00:55.513
Fuck!

00:56.765 --> 00:57.891
You bastard!

00:59.684 --> 01:01.436
Start the car!

01:02.937 --> 01:04.647
Hyeon-ju! Hurry up! Faster!

01:04.731 --> 01:05.565
Run faster!

01:08.443 --> 01:10.195
Hurry! Faster!

01:11.780 --> 01:13.198
Start the car!

01:15.075 --> 01:17.202
- Those bastards.
- Run faster!

01:17.285 --> 01:18.286
Hurry!

01:20.288 --> 01:22.290
Hurry up and get in!

01:22.373 --> 01:24.793
Close the door, Woo-jin. The door!

01:35.637 --> 01:37.263
Fuck.

02:00.745 --> 02:04.249
BLOODHOUNDS

02:05.083 --> 02:09.254
More people borrowed from Kim Myeong-gil
than we originally thought.

02:09.337 --> 02:13.091
People entered the bar
at one-hour intervals.

02:13.174 --> 02:15.635
Some of them came
in official police vehicles.

02:16.928 --> 02:18.179
I don't know the name,

02:18.888 --> 02:21.474
but there was a baseball player
I saw on TV.

02:23.268 --> 02:27.105
Yes, well, I'm sure he's expanded
his reach over the years.

02:45.832 --> 02:48.960
I knew Myeong-gil was an ex-convict.

02:49.669 --> 02:53.756
He said he wanted a fresh start
while working for me.

02:55.300 --> 02:56.885
He begged me desperately.

02:59.762 --> 03:00.930
And I fell for it.

03:03.266 --> 03:05.226
After Myeong-gil got me,

03:06.060 --> 03:08.521
I went into hiding in Namhae with Mr. Oh.

03:09.439 --> 03:11.900
That's when I heard rumors

03:12.859 --> 03:15.528
that Myeong-gil started a company
with my money and bonds.

03:17.113 --> 03:19.782
I should've been the one
to take care of him.

03:20.867 --> 03:22.785
I taught him, after all.

03:27.832 --> 03:29.334
But I didn't dare think about

03:31.002 --> 03:33.171
going after him.

03:35.757 --> 03:39.344
I stopped you
from going after Myeong-gil that time.

03:40.428 --> 03:41.387
I'm sorry for that.

03:42.847 --> 03:45.767
I was afraid I might lose you too.

03:52.857 --> 03:54.317
You have always

03:55.735 --> 03:58.404
cared for and protected me
as if I was family, sir.

04:00.531 --> 04:01.449
I am always ready

04:02.951 --> 04:06.120
to lay my life on the line for you, sir.

04:07.372 --> 04:08.331
Thank you.

04:10.625 --> 04:11.542
And I'm sorry.

04:20.843 --> 04:21.678
Yes.

04:23.513 --> 04:24.347
Is that so?

04:26.641 --> 04:27.725
I see. Hurry on over.

04:31.729 --> 04:35.358
Sir, it seems like the kids got jumped
by Kim Myeong-gil's men

04:35.942 --> 04:38.069
while getting the money
from the bookstore.

04:38.152 --> 04:38.987
Were they hurt?

04:39.070 --> 04:41.489
No, there was no mention of that, but…

04:43.658 --> 04:45.576
they lost all the money in the safe.

04:45.660 --> 04:47.287
Were they hurt or not?

04:48.162 --> 04:49.205
I think they're all right.

04:52.792 --> 04:55.920
Also, they tied
one of them up in the building,

04:56.004 --> 04:58.506
but they couldn't deal with him.
What should we do?

05:00.466 --> 05:03.970
Whenever an ER receives a patient
that was injured doing illegal activities,

05:04.887 --> 05:07.098
the doctors are obligated
to call the police.

05:07.849 --> 05:10.268
That's why I had an arrangement
with a hospital

05:10.768 --> 05:12.562
that was ready to operate at all times.

05:13.813 --> 05:16.399
Myeong-gil must have
a hospital of his own.

05:17.275 --> 05:19.652
I'll get Du-yeong on it.
A motorcycle will be useful.

06:11.662 --> 06:12.622
Good job.

06:14.123 --> 06:14.999
Hey.

06:18.586 --> 06:19.420
Good job.

06:20.546 --> 06:21.631
Right. Thank you.

06:22.715 --> 06:26.219
You kids get some sleep first.
Come to my restaurant at lunchtime.

06:27.428 --> 06:29.389
For what exactly do you…

06:30.390 --> 06:31.766
For food.

06:32.642 --> 06:33.476
I see.

06:35.436 --> 06:36.437
Do you not want to?

06:37.855 --> 06:39.399
I don't usually eat lunch.

06:39.482 --> 06:40.942
- Come.
- All right.

06:42.360 --> 06:43.319
Go on, then.

06:51.452 --> 06:52.286
Hey.

06:57.792 --> 06:58.793
Are you all right?

07:01.045 --> 07:03.840
We lost all the money
in the safe. I'm sorry.

07:03.923 --> 07:05.800
Did you get hurt?

07:08.428 --> 07:09.262
I'm all right.

07:10.596 --> 07:11.806
Then it's fine.

07:13.224 --> 07:17.270
Right. Let me finish moving the boxes.
You should go to sleep first.

07:21.941 --> 07:23.401
Are you sure you're not hurt?

07:28.030 --> 07:28.865
Yes.

08:23.294 --> 08:25.880
It's not that
I didn't pay them back. That guy…

08:27.548 --> 08:29.592
In-beom is mostly fine,

08:30.176 --> 08:31.969
but his right eardrum has ruptured.

08:33.137 --> 08:35.723
I'll run the plate number
I got from the dashcam in the morning.

08:36.682 --> 08:37.975
You still haven't done that?

08:39.101 --> 08:41.604
The police haven't come to work yet.

08:44.232 --> 08:45.608
I don't like your tone.

08:48.069 --> 08:49.111
I like those eyes.

08:49.779 --> 08:50.905
Damn it.

08:58.120 --> 09:01.457
If they used an unregistered vehicle
or fake plates,

09:01.541 --> 09:04.794
could you track how far it got
using security cameras?

09:06.295 --> 09:08.798
It's possible, but it'll take a while.

09:09.465 --> 09:12.260
License plates can be looked up
on the police Intranet easily.

09:12.843 --> 09:16.180
But you have to go to the control center
and look through CCTVs one by one.

09:16.764 --> 09:18.808
Each district has its own control center,

09:18.891 --> 09:20.977
so I need time to get the right people.

09:21.769 --> 09:24.939
Money isn't an issue,
so do it as soon as possible.

09:25.773 --> 09:26.607
Yes, sir.

09:26.691 --> 09:29.443
Find out who owns the building
the bookstore is in.

09:29.944 --> 09:32.655
If it's President Choi,
you'll be able to find his home address.

09:33.531 --> 09:34.365
Yes, sir.

09:34.448 --> 09:37.618
Let me talk to Jang-do in private.

09:39.203 --> 09:40.037
Excuse me?

09:42.373 --> 09:43.457
Didn't you hear me?

09:47.336 --> 09:48.421
Yes, sir.

10:09.483 --> 10:12.737
Why do you think
they just left Beom there?

10:14.530 --> 10:16.282
Maybe they were busy moving the money.

10:16.991 --> 10:19.452
Jang-do. Come on.

10:20.077 --> 10:23.039
Positive thinkers never improve.

10:23.664 --> 10:25.291
Think negatively for a change.

10:26.125 --> 10:29.128
Let the fear of those bastards

10:29.211 --> 10:31.547
doing everything
in their power to kill you

10:32.131 --> 10:33.549
drive your thoughts.

10:36.385 --> 10:37.678
To tail him?

10:40.723 --> 10:44.769
Allocate more men to the hospital.
Dress them up as patients and arm them.

10:45.603 --> 10:46.437
Yes, sir.

10:48.397 --> 10:49.857
Have guys tail Jun-min too.

10:52.693 --> 10:54.028
Did he do something wrong?

10:54.111 --> 10:57.281
Jeez. I told you to think negatively.

10:58.449 --> 11:01.577
President Choi may have gotten
his personal details.

11:02.620 --> 11:03.663
I see.

11:05.790 --> 11:09.502
Jun-min is a coward.
It'll be written all over his face.

11:10.169 --> 11:12.296
They might be able to tell
from a distance.

11:12.380 --> 11:14.340
It's best that
he's kept in the dark. Okay?

11:15.257 --> 11:16.092
Yes, sir.

11:17.927 --> 11:22.098
I don't think they'll put Hwang Yang-jung
on the job for a small fry like him.

11:22.598 --> 11:23.891
They'll send Lee Du-yeong.

11:23.974 --> 11:27.186
I told you how he covers
a wide distance on his bike.

11:27.269 --> 11:28.104
You did.

11:28.187 --> 11:31.065
Block off his point of entry
and exit, and get him.

11:33.234 --> 11:34.068
Yes, sir.

11:35.945 --> 11:37.071
This should be fun.

12:03.973 --> 12:05.099
Good morning, Mr. Choi.

12:05.850 --> 12:07.059
Did you get any sleep?

12:07.143 --> 12:08.644
Yes, I did.

12:08.728 --> 12:11.105
You got back so late. You should rest.

12:11.188 --> 12:12.857
I slept so deep that it was enough.

12:12.940 --> 12:13.983
Right. Gun-woo.

12:14.525 --> 12:16.277
I have something to talk to you about.

12:16.360 --> 12:17.194
I see.

12:22.324 --> 12:25.161
Hyeon-ju is a lonely child.

12:25.244 --> 12:27.705
There's always a shadow
lurking in her heart.

12:27.788 --> 12:28.622
I see.

12:29.582 --> 12:33.085
That's why she acts cold
on purpose at times.

12:33.753 --> 12:34.879
I see.

12:36.297 --> 12:39.884
But Hyeon-ju's brightened up considerably
after meeting you and Woo-jin.

12:39.967 --> 12:42.470
So I'm very thankful to you two.

12:43.721 --> 12:45.556
We also enjoy being with Hyeon-ju.

12:45.639 --> 12:49.143
Also, about the money
I paid you in advance,

12:50.144 --> 12:51.020
it's gone.

12:52.104 --> 12:53.647
I see.

12:53.731 --> 12:55.775
Where did it go?

12:55.858 --> 12:58.068
What I'm saying is we're even now.

12:58.152 --> 12:59.612
I see. Why is that?

12:59.695 --> 13:03.741
Do you know how much money you recovered
from the bookstore yesterday?

13:04.408 --> 13:05.743
Well…

13:10.623 --> 13:14.668
I'm giving you a bonus
for safely transporting my money.

13:14.752 --> 13:15.586
I see.

13:16.837 --> 13:19.548
I'd like to pay it back
by working off my debt.

13:19.632 --> 13:21.383
You've earned it.

13:22.551 --> 13:24.845
You all retrieved a considerable sum.

13:27.681 --> 13:30.935
Also, you are no longer indebted to me.

13:31.936 --> 13:36.440
Take your mother and open a new café
someplace nice, like Jeju Island.

13:37.983 --> 13:40.152
I'll make the necessary investments.

13:43.531 --> 13:45.866
Thank you so much, Mr. Choi.

13:46.367 --> 13:49.954
But I'd like to help you
catch Kim Myeong-gil

13:50.746 --> 13:52.081
to the very end.

13:52.164 --> 13:53.707
You've helped enough.

13:53.791 --> 13:56.418
Not at all. I would like to see this
through to the end.

13:57.920 --> 13:58.754
Why is that?

13:59.713 --> 14:00.965
I need to return the favor.

14:01.549 --> 14:03.008
You've done enough.

14:03.092 --> 14:04.718
It's not enough for me.

14:05.928 --> 14:08.097
It isn't over until it's over.

14:11.517 --> 14:12.393
I see.

14:14.270 --> 14:16.355
It's not over until it's over.

14:17.606 --> 14:19.859
Let's grab a drink sometime soon.

14:20.568 --> 14:22.945
Well, I don't drink.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.530
Jeez.

14:24.613 --> 14:26.532
But I can pour your drinks.

14:31.078 --> 14:32.580
- Go on upstairs.
- Yes, sir.

14:58.606 --> 15:00.900
Put some wasabi on it,
and have it with soy sauce.

15:22.004 --> 15:23.005
This is from the wild.

15:24.423 --> 15:25.841
You see, farmed halibut

15:25.925 --> 15:28.886
has a lot of fat in its fins
and can be a little too heavy.

15:28.969 --> 15:32.139
But wild ones like these
have a springy texture

15:32.222 --> 15:33.933
and even fat distribution.

15:34.558 --> 15:37.645
The unique, clean flavor of halibut
is absolutely…

15:39.688 --> 15:41.315
I can feel it every time I chew.

15:41.815 --> 15:43.150
It's also aged to perfection.

15:45.444 --> 15:47.821
Are you into sashimi?

15:47.905 --> 15:51.575
Well, I worked briefly as
a sashimi restaurant YouTuber back then.

15:51.659 --> 15:54.328
I quit because I couldn't get over
1,000 subscribers.

15:54.411 --> 15:57.706
Jeez. This is my first time eating
such a long cut.

15:57.790 --> 16:00.209
It wraps around in my mouth like a whip.

16:00.876 --> 16:03.671
This is the best halibut
I've ever had, sir.

16:04.713 --> 16:05.547
Like.

16:06.840 --> 16:08.258
Whoa, Woo-jin. You're amazing.

16:08.342 --> 16:10.636
Hey, I've worked hard in life.

16:10.719 --> 16:11.929
I'll subscribe.

16:12.012 --> 16:13.722
- I told you I quit.
- Right.

16:14.431 --> 16:18.060
You kids went through a lot yesterday,
so I wanted to treat you.

16:18.143 --> 16:19.603
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

16:19.687 --> 16:21.271
How will you proceed from here?

16:21.855 --> 16:23.357
We'll kill the big guy,

16:24.316 --> 16:27.027
and we'll catch the wildcat-looking one
and make him talk.

16:27.611 --> 16:30.155
That wildcat-looking bastard is
Kim Myeong-gil's cleanup guy.

16:31.281 --> 16:35.077
If I had to guess, he's the one
that goes around buying people's silence.

16:35.160 --> 16:38.205
Threatening them into submission
whenever Kim Myeong-gil causes trouble.

16:38.747 --> 16:39.665
After we fuck him up

16:40.374 --> 16:43.043
and find the body Kim Myeong-gil
made him bury, it's over.

16:43.127 --> 16:45.170
No amount of money
can make a dead body go away.

16:45.254 --> 16:47.256
I guess that would end Smile Capital.

16:47.339 --> 16:48.340
That's right.

16:49.299 --> 16:51.635
What do we look for
if we can't find the body?

16:51.719 --> 16:54.138
If we find a murder weapon
or the right footage,

16:54.221 --> 16:55.764
that would also end them.

16:57.766 --> 16:58.600
Here.

17:00.227 --> 17:01.937
As for the yellowtail,

17:02.771 --> 17:04.231
the aging process--

17:04.314 --> 17:05.941
I'm sorry.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.569
- Sit.
- You sure took your time.

17:09.111 --> 17:11.488
Hello, I'm Lee Du-yeong.
I've heard about you guys.

17:11.572 --> 17:13.490
- I'm Kim Gun-woo, sir.
- Okay.

17:13.574 --> 17:14.908
- I'm Hong Woo-jin, sir.
- Jeez.

17:14.992 --> 17:17.494
Boxers' fists are built differently.
Nice to meet you.

17:18.078 --> 17:20.748
I actually went
to the underground passage that day.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.710
I went over right after the boss called,
but I live far away, so I was late.

17:24.793 --> 17:27.379
But then I saw those goons
all lying on the ground

17:27.463 --> 17:30.090
and thought,
"These kids are real fighters."

17:30.174 --> 17:31.050
I see.

17:32.051 --> 17:35.679
You also dreamed of becoming
a world champion back in the day, right?

17:35.763 --> 17:37.848
Why are you dragging me into this?

17:37.931 --> 17:38.766
Why not?

17:40.350 --> 17:41.351
Can you go on a hit today?

17:42.853 --> 17:45.355
- What?
- The sales director.

17:45.439 --> 17:47.066
We'll talk when we're alone.

17:47.149 --> 17:49.526
Why? They're coming with us.

17:50.027 --> 17:51.820
What do you mean they're coming too?

17:51.904 --> 17:54.740
- What's the issue?
- I don't want them to be accomplices.

17:56.533 --> 17:59.286
They're the ones who wanted in.
Don't take it out on me.

18:01.830 --> 18:03.665
Hey. Once you have a criminal record,

18:03.749 --> 18:06.168
you can't return to the ring.
You know that, right?

18:06.752 --> 18:08.003
Yes.

18:10.756 --> 18:13.008
Why are you fighting Kim Myeong-gil?

18:13.092 --> 18:15.344
I have to avenge our boys' deaths.

18:15.427 --> 18:18.347
You could die fighting Kim Myeong-gil.

18:18.430 --> 18:19.264
Aren't you afraid?

18:19.848 --> 18:20.933
I'm not afraid of dying.

18:21.433 --> 18:23.060
I'm afraid of not killing them.

18:25.437 --> 18:26.730
What will you guys do?

18:26.814 --> 18:28.690
- I'm going.
- Me too.

18:28.774 --> 18:29.817
Why?

18:30.442 --> 18:32.569
Kim Myeong-gil is a terrible man.

18:33.570 --> 18:36.657
Our family would've been ruined
if it weren't for Mr. Choi.

18:37.491 --> 18:39.618
The only thing I'm good at is fighting,

18:40.244 --> 18:42.079
but I want to help until the very end.

18:42.955 --> 18:43.872
Same here.

18:43.956 --> 18:46.458
We, the Marine duo,
can be of great assistance.

18:46.542 --> 18:47.918
You guys are Marines?

18:48.001 --> 18:48.836
Yes, sir.

18:49.378 --> 18:50.379
Are you a Marine, sir?

18:50.963 --> 18:52.798
I was exempted, but he was a Marine.

18:53.924 --> 18:54.758
Hey.

18:55.509 --> 18:56.760
Salute!

18:59.263 --> 19:00.264
Salute.

19:01.265 --> 19:04.560
Why do you keep divulging
my personal information? Are you crazy?

19:04.643 --> 19:07.187
This is how you get to know each other.

19:09.731 --> 19:11.316
Put those hands down, you punks.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.526
Tell us your class, sir!

19:13.360 --> 19:14.194
I said put them down.

19:16.029 --> 19:17.614
I wish to call you a senior Marine, sir!

19:18.907 --> 19:22.119
Look at this punk, making me get up.
I said hands down, you fool!

19:24.037 --> 19:26.331
Once a Marine, always a Marine, sir!

19:26.415 --> 19:29.209
- Would you look at that?
- Go easy on him.

19:29.293 --> 19:32.171
This punk is trying to one-up me.
Look at this guy.

19:32.671 --> 19:35.090
No, sir. It's the Marine spirit
that's one-upping you.

19:35.174 --> 19:38.177
Sir, he's a bit high on pride.

19:38.260 --> 19:39.970
Please let him off the hook.

19:40.554 --> 19:41.471
"High on pride"?

19:42.055 --> 19:43.974
It means his MCP's a bit strong.

19:44.057 --> 19:45.184
What's "MCP"?

19:45.267 --> 19:47.811
- It's short for Marine Corps Pride.
- I see.

19:47.895 --> 19:49.354
Please tell me your class, sir.

19:49.938 --> 19:51.565
Yang-jung, he's high on MCP.

19:51.648 --> 19:53.025
Please tell me, sir!

19:55.444 --> 19:58.238
I'm class 571. Are you happy now?

20:00.282 --> 20:01.158
Senior Marine.

20:01.658 --> 20:03.118
Salute!

20:09.166 --> 20:10.000
Are you going too?

20:11.585 --> 20:13.337
Do you think I can't put up a fight?

20:14.838 --> 20:16.381
The boss might worry.

20:17.132 --> 20:18.217
That's why I asked.

20:19.509 --> 20:22.596
I started this.
I'll see it through to the end.

20:23.597 --> 20:24.431
Okay.

20:26.934 --> 20:27.768
Okay.

20:28.936 --> 20:30.437
We'll strike tonight.

20:30.938 --> 20:33.273
Du-yeong, call me
once you get the sales director.

20:33.357 --> 20:36.109
I'll wait in front of the hospital
and move in once you call.

20:36.193 --> 20:37.069
Understood.

20:37.569 --> 20:39.238
Why wait to go in?

20:39.321 --> 20:41.406
If there are goons
with the sales director,

20:41.490 --> 20:44.201
they've caught on.
That means they'll be at the hospital too.

20:45.285 --> 20:47.746
Wouldn't it be dangerous
for Mr. Lee to go alone?

20:48.330 --> 20:49.498
He'll be fine. He's fast.

20:51.333 --> 20:52.834
Wouldn't it be safer

20:52.918 --> 20:55.963
to gang up on Kim Jun-min together,
then go in and get Im Jang-do?

20:56.713 --> 20:58.674
Once he knows that we're on the move,

20:58.757 --> 21:00.968
Kim Myeong-gil will unleash
all of his goons.

21:01.510 --> 21:02.511
Then we're dead.

21:02.594 --> 21:04.388
The numbers aren't in our favor.

21:04.888 --> 21:07.599
We have to split up
and hit them simultaneously.

21:08.558 --> 21:09.559
It's dangerous,

21:09.643 --> 21:11.645
but that's the only way we'll win.

21:14.856 --> 21:16.692
I'm on a motorcycle, so I'll be fine.

21:17.192 --> 21:19.069
I'll run if things get dicey.

21:21.780 --> 21:23.115
What should we do?

21:24.491 --> 21:25.701
Can you ride a motorcycle?

21:26.493 --> 21:27.327
No.

21:27.828 --> 21:29.288
A scooter is fast too.

21:29.871 --> 21:30.706
What?

21:31.623 --> 21:32.749
Nothing, sir.

21:34.042 --> 21:37.004
I'll bring them with me.
I might need them at the hospital.

21:38.005 --> 21:40.882
I'll go with Mr. Lee.
I can ride a motorcycle.

21:42.009 --> 21:42.843
All right.

21:43.677 --> 21:44.511
Now, shall we eat?

21:45.095 --> 21:45.929
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

21:46.430 --> 21:47.973
Hyeon-ju, you ride a motorcycle?

21:48.557 --> 21:49.725
- Yes.
- What kind?

21:50.225 --> 21:51.518
I ride a naked bike.

21:52.394 --> 21:54.396
Don't you think we look a bit similar?

21:55.605 --> 21:56.606
- Right?
- Yes.

21:57.649 --> 21:58.483
Damn it.

21:58.567 --> 22:00.235
Hey, no need to curse.

22:00.319 --> 22:01.445
Where'd you serve, sir?

22:01.528 --> 22:03.155
Let's not talk about the military.

22:03.864 --> 22:05.032
You should stop.

22:05.741 --> 22:08.702
Hey, Min-dong. Give us some soup and rice.

22:09.536 --> 22:10.370
Yes, sir.

22:12.331 --> 22:13.165
Duk.

22:13.665 --> 22:15.792
- How have you been?
- Great. It's been a while, sir.

22:16.293 --> 22:17.377
She'll be riding it.

22:17.461 --> 22:18.545
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:19.379 --> 22:20.797
I've prepared it over there.

22:23.133 --> 22:24.593
The new ones are nice.

22:26.887 --> 22:30.098
- Did you ever ride a racing model before?
- Briefly, a while back.

22:31.475 --> 22:35.062
You were trained
on how to hold a knife in the army, right?

22:35.145 --> 22:36.855
- Try holding this.
- No.

22:37.898 --> 22:38.732
No?

22:38.815 --> 22:39.900
- No.
- No.

22:43.904 --> 22:44.946
Try holding it anyway.

22:45.030 --> 22:48.575
Sir, we don't plan on using knives.

22:50.243 --> 22:53.413
- Who told you to use a knife?
- Well, didn't you just offer us knives?

22:53.997 --> 22:55.207
Are you talking back?

22:55.290 --> 22:56.500
I'll do better, sir!

22:59.127 --> 23:02.881
You have to know how to use a knife
in order to know how a knifer thinks.

23:02.964 --> 23:04.925
You have to read their minds to beat them.

23:05.008 --> 23:06.134
I see.

23:06.718 --> 23:07.803
Jeez. That scared me.

23:10.097 --> 23:12.224
Let's see. Once you get used to it…

23:14.434 --> 23:15.685
This is the fastest one.

23:23.360 --> 23:24.319
It suits you.

23:25.695 --> 23:29.950
Sashimi knives don't have a guard
between the hilt and blade.

23:30.033 --> 23:31.827
This blade isn't for stabbing.

23:32.744 --> 23:34.871
Look. If you stab hard with this…

23:36.498 --> 23:39.501
your hand slides forward,
and the blade will fuck up your fingers.

23:39.584 --> 23:41.002
To stab deep with this,

23:41.086 --> 23:42.796
you have to support the back.

23:43.463 --> 23:44.297
That's how

23:45.715 --> 23:46.675
your hands don't slip.

23:48.385 --> 23:50.804
If someone's like this,
what are they aiming for?

23:50.887 --> 23:53.390
They're trying to slash my hand or wrist.

23:53.473 --> 23:56.101
Correct. It won't exactly cut deep.

23:56.685 --> 24:00.021
In boxing, it's like
when an out-boxer throws light jabs.

24:00.105 --> 24:01.398
I see!

24:04.693 --> 24:05.902
One more time!

24:05.986 --> 24:06.820
It's fine.

24:07.988 --> 24:09.906
Loosen up and keep circling around.

24:18.457 --> 24:20.834
What if they're supporting
with both hands?

24:20.917 --> 24:23.170
They're coming in for the kill, right?

24:25.589 --> 24:28.175
Since you're pushing down with your thumb,

24:28.258 --> 24:30.343
your hand won't slide easily.

24:31.136 --> 24:34.139
If someone holds their knife like this,
they're experienced.

24:34.222 --> 24:36.641
Swing with the same speed
you're coming in at.

24:36.725 --> 24:37.851
- With less force.
- Lightly.

24:37.934 --> 24:38.894
- Like this.
- Right.

24:47.110 --> 24:48.153
That's it!

25:01.750 --> 25:03.502
Play dirty, and I'll kill you.

25:04.294 --> 25:06.087
What are you doing? Start dealing.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.215
- Fuck. Let me have this.
- Hey, show me.

25:10.759 --> 25:11.927
Where are your manners?

25:18.767 --> 25:20.810
You fucking pricks!

25:39.120 --> 25:40.372
Let's wait here.

26:05.564 --> 26:06.690
Stop!

26:07.732 --> 26:10.068
- Which unit are you visiting?
- Unit 603.

26:12.737 --> 26:14.072
A car is coming in.

26:31.214 --> 26:32.257
We have one.

26:32.882 --> 26:33.717
What do we do?

26:35.635 --> 26:36.469
Wait for now.

26:41.266 --> 26:42.851
INCOMING CALL

26:42.934 --> 26:44.394
Damn it.

27:06.207 --> 27:07.042
Thank you, sir.

27:08.043 --> 27:09.044
Listen while drinking.

27:09.127 --> 27:11.129
In order to survive in this line of work,

27:11.713 --> 27:13.340
you have to sell everything you've got.

27:14.257 --> 27:15.550
Your fists.

27:15.634 --> 27:16.509
Your soul.

27:17.010 --> 27:17.844
Your dreams.

27:18.595 --> 27:19.888
Sell it, and you'll live.

27:21.181 --> 27:23.850
However, don't sell out
your friends and family.

27:23.933 --> 27:25.852
It's better to die than to live like that.

27:27.437 --> 27:28.271
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

27:29.898 --> 27:31.566
When I go into the hospital

27:31.650 --> 27:34.152
and tell you guys to run,
don't argue with me. Just run.

27:34.235 --> 27:36.071
I'll take care of things inside.

27:38.823 --> 27:40.075
Got it?

27:41.159 --> 27:45.205
Didn't you just tell us
not to abandon our friends and family?

27:45.789 --> 27:46.956
I'm a criminal.

27:47.040 --> 27:50.418
We may be in the same boat right now,
but we're not family.

27:50.502 --> 27:52.629
We'll never meet again
once this job's over.

27:52.712 --> 27:55.757
So don't think about getting
emotionally attached. Got it?

28:01.554 --> 28:02.639
Do you understand?

28:03.515 --> 28:04.349
Yes, sir.

28:06.685 --> 28:07.519
Yes, sir.

28:26.579 --> 28:27.664
Kim Jun-min is here.

28:33.461 --> 28:34.796
What are you going to do?

28:36.506 --> 28:38.341
Mr. Lee, what do we do?

28:39.342 --> 28:40.301
Can you hear me?

28:40.927 --> 28:42.262
Please answer me.

28:42.762 --> 28:43.805
I'm going in.

29:00.405 --> 29:02.282
This motherfucker!

29:14.711 --> 29:15.754
Call the hospital!

29:32.771 --> 29:35.398
You son of a bitch! Motherfucker!

29:36.900 --> 29:37.901
Die!

29:37.984 --> 29:40.236
Motherfucker! You son of a bitch!

29:40.320 --> 29:43.239
Fuck, you son of a bitch!

29:45.492 --> 29:46.367
Do-hu.

29:46.451 --> 29:48.953
Put this fucker in the trunk.

29:49.537 --> 29:50.914
Hurry up and put him in!

29:54.459 --> 29:55.293
What the hell?

29:57.420 --> 29:59.214
- What the hell!
- That son of a bitch!

30:05.553 --> 30:06.971
- Son of a bitch.
- Hey!

30:21.986 --> 30:22.821
Are you all right?

30:41.047 --> 30:42.632
MAIN BUILDING
PATIENT ROOM, BLOCK 17

30:42.715 --> 30:44.843
DU-YEONG

30:46.719 --> 30:47.637
Yes.

30:50.098 --> 30:50.974
Are you all right?

30:52.225 --> 30:53.059
Okay.

31:02.569 --> 31:03.403
Let's go.

31:04.153 --> 31:05.280
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

31:40.398 --> 31:41.232
It's Im Jang-do.

31:46.863 --> 31:48.573
BITCOIN

31:48.656 --> 31:50.408
That's right, up you go.

31:54.704 --> 31:55.538
Damn it!

32:06.090 --> 32:07.675
Come on! Let's go!

32:07.759 --> 32:09.052
Fuck!

32:23.441 --> 32:24.275
All right. Wait.

32:25.944 --> 32:26.861
Just a second.

32:27.528 --> 32:28.655
Let me go. Damn it!

32:32.283 --> 32:33.201
Damn it.

32:36.704 --> 32:37.997
Who the fuck are you?

33:08.027 --> 33:09.237
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir.

33:15.284 --> 33:16.202
Be careful.

33:38.307 --> 33:41.394
WE'VE GOT IM JANG-DO
TAKING HIM TO DU-YEONG'S STORE

33:59.954 --> 34:01.372
- You're here.
- Hello, sir.

34:09.839 --> 34:10.840
Can you put him here?

34:10.923 --> 34:11.841
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

34:14.135 --> 34:15.261
One, two…

34:15.344 --> 34:16.345
Be careful.

34:16.846 --> 34:18.097
Jeez.

34:19.474 --> 34:20.600
Where's the salt?

34:20.683 --> 34:21.517
Salt?

34:23.102 --> 34:24.062
It's in the office.

34:25.188 --> 34:26.397
Go make some salt water.

34:27.607 --> 34:29.567
Find a bucket and pour in all the salt.

34:29.650 --> 34:30.777
Yes, sir.

34:30.860 --> 34:31.944
- Let's go.
- Okay.

34:32.028 --> 34:32.987
It's by the corner.

34:33.071 --> 34:33.988
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

34:35.490 --> 34:36.532
Damn it.

34:43.664 --> 34:45.083
Hyeon-ju, are you all right?

34:45.166 --> 34:46.918
Yes. Are you all right?

34:47.001 --> 34:47.960
Yes.

34:49.670 --> 34:51.672
We've got Im Jang-do.

34:52.173 --> 34:53.466
- Right.
- And Kim Jun-min?

34:53.549 --> 34:56.344
Well, I was outside so I couldn't see,
but he said he got him.

34:56.427 --> 34:59.472
- I see.
- Did he kill him by chance?

35:05.728 --> 35:07.230
Let's hurry and make salt water.

35:07.313 --> 35:08.731
- Go find it.
- Right.

35:13.111 --> 35:14.445
I think we can use this.

35:14.529 --> 35:16.030
- And water?
- I saw it downstairs.

35:16.114 --> 35:16.948
Let's head down.

35:17.031 --> 35:18.157
Hyeon-ju, let's go.

35:32.797 --> 35:33.756
Yes, sir.

35:33.840 --> 35:36.676
I'll be arriving in five minutes,
so shake him up a bit.

35:36.759 --> 35:38.010
Also,

35:39.095 --> 35:41.180
have Hyeon-ju and the other kids watch.

35:55.528 --> 35:56.362
What is it?

35:58.197 --> 35:59.824
He wants Hyeon-ju to watch.

35:59.907 --> 36:00.867
Why?

36:03.619 --> 36:05.413
Man. Will Hyeon-ju be all right?

36:07.415 --> 36:09.167
Hello, sir. Right this way.

36:25.099 --> 36:26.184
Let's see the stairs.

36:26.267 --> 36:27.894
We don't have cameras on that side.

36:28.519 --> 36:29.353
Why not?

36:29.437 --> 36:30.771
We just don't.

36:33.316 --> 36:34.817
Are you fucking kidding me?

36:35.776 --> 36:40.281
Well, are there any cameras outside
facing the building?

36:40.865 --> 36:42.783
You'll have to go to the police for that.

36:51.542 --> 36:52.376
How's Jun-min?

36:54.378 --> 36:55.588
He's unconscious, sir.

36:56.797 --> 36:58.299
Go to the apartment manager,

36:58.382 --> 37:00.343
and find the bastards that got Jun-min.

37:00.843 --> 37:01.677
Yes, sir.

37:03.095 --> 37:05.139
- Let's put it here.
- I'll pour it in.

37:05.223 --> 37:06.349
How much do we pour?

37:06.849 --> 37:09.018
Didn't he tell us to pour in everything?

37:09.101 --> 37:10.228
Isn't this too much?

37:11.562 --> 37:13.481
Let's pour in everything.
You answered him.

37:14.398 --> 37:15.441
All right.

37:18.736 --> 37:19.612
What are you doing?

37:19.695 --> 37:21.155
They told us to make salt water.

37:26.953 --> 37:27.870
Right, salt water.

37:27.954 --> 37:29.080
Yes, sir.

37:33.209 --> 37:34.502
Come here and watch.

37:36.170 --> 37:37.004
Why?

37:37.088 --> 37:38.673
It's Mr. Choi's orders.

37:46.472 --> 37:50.184
I hate when people open their mouths
and then close them again.

37:51.310 --> 37:55.773
So when you find the resolve
to tell me everything, nod your head.

37:57.275 --> 38:01.028
If you say you'll talk and then back down,
I'll carve your lips off with a knife.

38:01.612 --> 38:02.446
Got it?

38:40.651 --> 38:42.236
You're not going to talk, are you?

39:49.720 --> 39:50.721
Hyeon-ju.

40:05.152 --> 40:06.695
Why did you tell me to watch that?

40:07.488 --> 40:10.616
Myeong-gil probably started looking
for Im Jang-do by now.

40:10.699 --> 40:12.660
We don't have much time.

40:13.494 --> 40:16.288
There's something
I want to teach you guys.

40:17.123 --> 40:18.499
What are you talking about?

40:18.582 --> 40:21.252
This won't end until someone dies.

40:21.335 --> 40:23.754
And there's no guarantee
that I'll make it out alive.

40:23.838 --> 40:27.174
Then win. Why are you so fixated
on the worst outcome?

40:27.258 --> 40:29.343
- Hyeon-ju.
- That's enough.

40:35.141 --> 40:36.100
Hyeon-ju!

40:39.478 --> 40:41.105
Mr. Oh, please go after Hyeon-ju.

40:41.188 --> 40:42.189
Yes, sir.

40:43.399 --> 40:45.109
Jeez. That kid, seriously.

40:49.155 --> 40:50.906
- Gun-woo.
- Yes, sir.

40:52.825 --> 40:53.701
If…

40:55.744 --> 40:57.163
Myeong-gil and you guys

40:58.164 --> 41:00.166
end up fighting,

41:01.292 --> 41:03.127
can you protect the others?

41:04.962 --> 41:06.422
I'll protect them to the end.

41:07.882 --> 41:08.924
Okay, thank you.

41:10.593 --> 41:14.638
We don't have much time,
so let me teach you just one thing.

41:18.225 --> 41:22.354
You need two things
to beat a tight-knit organization.

41:24.273 --> 41:26.650
Dispersion and division.

41:28.319 --> 41:31.030
People tend to trust those
that know them well

41:31.113 --> 41:32.490
and empathize with them.

41:34.575 --> 41:36.827
Without gaining an individual's trust,

41:38.287 --> 41:40.331
you can't hope to divide an organization.

41:55.387 --> 41:56.305
Take it off.

42:13.197 --> 42:14.073
Im Jang-do?

42:15.115 --> 42:17.660
I believe that you,
of all Myeong-gil's men,

42:17.743 --> 42:20.788
have the best understanding of the man.

42:21.997 --> 42:24.917
Myeong-gil is a very violent
and cruel man.

42:25.000 --> 42:27.586
But he's capable
of reading people like a book.

42:28.671 --> 42:30.256
He also knows how to win them over.

42:31.090 --> 42:35.219
So Kim Jun-min and Kang In-beom
probably believe in him in earnest.

42:35.928 --> 42:37.346
But you're a smart man.

42:37.846 --> 42:39.723
You know Myeong-gil better than them.

42:40.641 --> 42:43.102
Myeong-gil never truly empathizes
with anything

42:43.185 --> 42:44.812
from the bottom of his heart.

42:45.312 --> 42:47.106
He empathizes coldly with his head.

42:47.815 --> 42:52.236
He's always calculating
how to manipulate people to his advantage.

42:52.319 --> 42:55.781
Yet knowing this,
you still went to work for him.

42:56.448 --> 42:57.449
Why?

42:58.576 --> 43:00.494
The first reason was money.

43:02.079 --> 43:04.415
Myeong-gil paid you in a year
what a major corporation

43:04.498 --> 43:06.625
would have paid you
for five years of work.

43:06.709 --> 43:10.087
Graduating from Police University
was your ticket to authority,

43:10.170 --> 43:12.673
but you were demoted.
Making money was your only option.

43:12.756 --> 43:15.092
That's how you'd save your pride.

43:17.344 --> 43:21.390
But the second reason is why
you really decided to work for Myeong-gil.

43:21.974 --> 43:25.185
You were confident
you wouldn't let Myeong-gil use you.

43:25.769 --> 43:29.815
You were certain you wouldn't lose
to a criminal bastard like him.

43:30.816 --> 43:33.652
And if Myeong-gil ever found
a reason to kill you,

43:33.736 --> 43:37.156
all you had to do was hightail it
to Southeast Asia

43:38.115 --> 43:40.200
with the money you made
working for Myeong-gil.

43:43.495 --> 43:45.289
I really like your plan.

43:46.457 --> 43:50.586
But if I were to take your photo now
and send it to Myeong-gil,

43:52.046 --> 43:55.466
telling him that you ratted out
the people Myeong-gil had you kill,

43:55.549 --> 43:57.259
he'd trust me without a doubt

43:57.343 --> 44:01.597
because your current state
is motive enough for you to squeal.

44:04.183 --> 44:08.312
Then Myeong-gil will call back
the men he sent out to find you

44:08.395 --> 44:12.733
and unleash a pack of bloodhounds
to kill and dispose of you discretely.

44:13.734 --> 44:17.363
Those guys won't give you time
to plead your case to Myeong-gil

44:17.446 --> 44:18.989
because he told them not to.

44:19.073 --> 44:21.492
Myeong-gil isn't interested in the truth.

44:21.992 --> 44:24.536
It's safest to bury you six feet under.

44:24.620 --> 44:29.291
I mean, the person who knows
Myeong-gil's crimes best

44:29.375 --> 44:32.211
isn't Kim Jun-min
or Kang In-beom. It's you.

44:36.757 --> 44:38.967
You know Myeong-gil as well as I do.

44:40.511 --> 44:45.140
If I were to plant even the smallest seed
of doubt in his mind about you…

44:47.768 --> 44:49.353
Myeong-gil would kill you.

44:49.978 --> 44:50.854
Fuck.

44:53.065 --> 44:53.982
Wait.

44:55.150 --> 44:56.527
Why should I die?

44:58.112 --> 44:59.446
Fuck!

44:59.530 --> 45:00.406
Im Jang-do!

45:02.032 --> 45:03.826
Listen to me carefully!

45:03.909 --> 45:06.537
If you don't pull yourself together now,
you'll really die!

45:11.417 --> 45:13.085
Tell me everything you know.

45:14.586 --> 45:17.506
In exchange, I'll send you off
to a safe country

45:17.589 --> 45:19.550
with enough money
for the rest of your life.

45:20.551 --> 45:22.428
Myeong-gil learned everything from me.

45:23.804 --> 45:26.432
I know of places he hasn't even heard of.

45:27.057 --> 45:28.142
I promise.

45:32.020 --> 45:35.107
You were going to make an exit anyway.

45:36.525 --> 45:38.110
Now is your chance.

45:43.824 --> 45:44.783
If I tell you,

45:46.493 --> 45:47.828
how much will you give me?

45:50.998 --> 45:52.750
Answer quickly and sincerely.

45:59.965 --> 46:03.135
I'm going to end
Myeong-gil and Smile Capital for good.

46:04.136 --> 46:05.721
After that, I'll send you to Guam.

46:05.804 --> 46:07.389
I know some people there.

46:08.182 --> 46:11.810
I'll give you all the backing you need
to start a new life there.

46:20.444 --> 46:21.528
Get him some clothes.

46:36.668 --> 46:38.378
How long have you worked for Myeong-gil?

46:39.463 --> 46:40.506
Five years.

46:40.589 --> 46:42.341
What exactly do you do?

46:42.925 --> 46:46.595
I make sure Mr. Kim's illegal dealings
fly under the police radar,

46:46.678 --> 46:50.182
keeping them from blowing up
if the police start investigating.

46:50.265 --> 46:51.809
And your personal contributions?

46:51.892 --> 46:54.353
For small cases,
In-beom and I'd go to take care of it,

46:54.853 --> 46:57.523
but for most cases,
we used Mr. Kim's service company.

46:58.148 --> 46:59.399
"Small cases"?

46:59.483 --> 47:00.317
Like…

47:01.944 --> 47:03.987
Things like filming dirt to use on others.

47:04.071 --> 47:06.406
You threatened Iil Group, didn't you?

47:09.243 --> 47:10.244
What did you do?

47:11.411 --> 47:12.913
Mr. Kim made me do it.

47:12.996 --> 47:15.707
He didn't ask you who.
He asked you what you did.

47:17.709 --> 47:19.711
I got footage of Iil Group's heir.

47:19.795 --> 47:20.921
What kind?

47:21.713 --> 47:23.173
We stripped him down

47:24.049 --> 47:25.342
and took videos.

47:25.425 --> 47:26.260
Why?

47:28.971 --> 47:31.056
Fill me in from the start.

47:32.724 --> 47:35.686
There's a 40-story posh hotel
being constructed in Gangnam.

47:35.769 --> 47:38.647
But after COVID-19 hit,
the company in charge went bankrupt.

47:39.690 --> 47:41.567
The Iil Group heir planned to take over,

47:41.650 --> 47:43.944
but Mr. Kim heard
they were 100 billion short.

47:44.027 --> 47:45.279
From who?

47:45.946 --> 47:47.906
The building was discarded for so long,

47:47.990 --> 47:49.491
Seoul City stepped in.

47:49.575 --> 47:51.535
They were looking for someone with cash,

47:51.618 --> 47:53.871
and an assemblyman
who plays golf with Mr. Kim

47:53.954 --> 47:56.456
recommended him to the mayor.

47:57.124 --> 48:01.169
Mr. Kim dreams
of building a casino in a hotel.

48:03.213 --> 48:06.383
Seoul City said they'd grant him
a permit for a foreigner-only casino,

48:06.884 --> 48:08.343
so Mr. Kim got excited.

48:08.427 --> 48:10.554
But the Iil Group heir tried to back out,

48:10.637 --> 48:13.056
so Mr. Kim made me get him to cooperate.

48:13.932 --> 48:16.184
How many people did you take videos of?

48:16.935 --> 48:17.769
Fifty.

48:19.187 --> 48:21.481
Is Myeong-gil holding on to these videos?

48:21.565 --> 48:22.399
Yes.

48:23.358 --> 48:25.819
He sees every weakness
as a source of income.

48:26.737 --> 48:27.779
Also,

48:28.363 --> 48:30.908
he never shares anything
that's worth any money.

48:31.575 --> 48:33.368
Where is this data?

48:35.287 --> 48:38.373
Mr. Kim keeps a hard drive
in a small safe inside his bedroom,

48:38.957 --> 48:41.001
but the safe is a German smart safe.

48:41.501 --> 48:44.087
It only opens by putting the vein
in his right arm against it.

48:44.171 --> 48:47.090
Should any issues arise, he can incinerate

48:47.174 --> 48:49.343
all of its contents remotely
using his phone.

48:49.426 --> 48:51.845
The top of the safe holds liquid fuel

48:51.929 --> 48:54.723
that will drop down
and ignite at the press of a button.

48:54.806 --> 48:57.309
He knows that the hard drive is
a double-edged sword.

48:57.392 --> 49:01.229
It's a weapon to him
but evidence to the police.

49:02.856 --> 49:05.442
That service company is a gang?

49:05.984 --> 49:06.818
Yes.

49:07.361 --> 49:08.195
How many men?

49:08.779 --> 49:12.157
I believe about 30,
but they call more if needed.

49:12.240 --> 49:13.325
Who's in charge?

49:13.909 --> 49:17.579
Mr. Jung, the president.
He's Mr. Kim's butcher.

49:17.663 --> 49:19.539
He used to be an MMA fighter,

49:19.623 --> 49:22.709
but he got banned for beating
a fighter to death during a match.

49:22.793 --> 49:24.670
I heard Mr. Kim recruited him.

49:24.753 --> 49:26.380
How do they get rid of the bodies?

49:27.130 --> 49:28.966
Mr. Jung takes care of the bodies.

49:29.466 --> 49:31.134
Yes, tell me what you know.

49:32.594 --> 49:36.682
About three years ago,
Mr. Kim saw red while drinking

49:36.765 --> 49:38.183
and beat a person to death.

49:39.142 --> 49:40.894
I happened to be nearby at the time,

49:40.978 --> 49:43.730
so I took care of things
until Mr. Jung got there.

49:43.814 --> 49:47.067
Mr. Jung called over a 3-ton fish truck
with an aquarium attached

49:47.150 --> 49:48.443
and carried the body away.

49:48.527 --> 49:52.155
From the way he was talking to the driver,
Mr. Jung seemed to be a regular.

49:53.031 --> 49:53.907
Do you have a name?

49:55.617 --> 49:57.160
It's been too long to remember.

49:59.121 --> 49:59.955
I see.

50:00.747 --> 50:02.416
I know a hospital in Incheon.

50:02.916 --> 50:05.252
I'll call over their ambulance,
so get some rest.

50:05.335 --> 50:08.422
Once the job's done
and everything's taken care of,

50:09.006 --> 50:10.924
I'll arrange a passport
and flight for you.

50:15.137 --> 50:16.930
Don't contact anyone.

50:18.098 --> 50:19.975
Otherwise, Kim Myeong-gil will find you.

50:24.771 --> 50:26.690
I'm taking your phone.

50:34.072 --> 50:35.782
Let me ask one last thing.

50:37.701 --> 50:39.870
Where's Myeong-gil's stash of gold?

50:41.705 --> 50:43.248
Only In-beom knows about that.

50:44.624 --> 50:45.834
What's their relationship?

50:45.917 --> 50:48.462
In-beom is the only person Mr. Kim trusts.

50:49.004 --> 50:51.089
They met in prison.

50:51.173 --> 50:53.425
I heard they saved
each other's lives many times.

50:53.508 --> 50:55.802
In-beom is willing to die for him.

50:56.928 --> 50:58.889
I don't know all of Mr. Kim's thoughts,

50:59.473 --> 51:01.933
but he thinks of In-beom
as his brother. I'm sure.
